    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of everything applied when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`, traced through the actual code.\n\n## Phase 0 \u2014 Servlet filter (before the controller)\n\n1. **Idempotency replay** (`IdempotentOwnerCreateFilter`): if the request carries an `Idempotency-Key` header and that key was already seen, the cached prior response body is replayed as `200 OK` and the request short-circuits. Otherwise the request proceeds and, if the eventual response is 2xx, the body is cached under that key.\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Authorization\n\n2. **`@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`** on `addOwner` \u2014 requires role `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`. *Only enforced when `petclinic.security.enable=true`; otherwise not applied.*\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Request binding & validation (on `OwnerFieldsDto`, before the method body)\n\nBoth the JSR-380 bean constraints **and** the custom `OwnerFieldsValidator` (wired in via `@InitBinder`) run against the same `BindingResult`; any failure \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 **400**.\n\n3. **Bean Validation constraints** on the DTO fields:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words)\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `title` `@Size(max 10)`; `address` `@Size(1..255)`; `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `email`: `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`\n   - `postcode`: `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")`\n\n4. **`OwnerFieldsValidator`** (runs and **mutates the DTO** as it validates, in this order):\n   - a. Composes `address` from `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` (or falls back to `address`), via `AddressNormalizer` (trim/collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST\u2192STREET etc.) \u2014 **sets `address`**.\n   - b. Rejects blank/whitespace-only `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone`.\n   - c. Normalizes `telephone` to E.164 (strips separators, defaults country code to `+61`, drops leading 0); if valid (`E164Telephone`) **sets `telephone`** to the normalized value, else rejects.\n   - d. Lower-cases `email` (**sets `email`**), then rejects disposable-email domains (mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com).\n   - e. Validates postcode is within the city's regional range (Sydney 2000\u20132099, Melbourne 3000\u20133099, Brisbane 4000\u20134099).\n   - f. Rejects `registrationDate` in the future.\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 Controller method body (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`)\n\n5. **Map** DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity (uses the values mutated in phase 2).\n6. **Load** all non-deleted owners (separate read transaction).\n7. **Daily registration limit**: if \u2265100 owners already registered today \u2192 **429 Too Many Requests** (short-circuits).\n8. **Assign `householdId`** (SHA-256 over normalized last name + postcode).\n9. **Hard-duplicate / capacity check**: if an existing owner shares the identity key (telephone + lower email + Soundex last name) **OR** the city already holds \u226550 owners \u2192 **409 Conflict** (short-circuits).\n10. **Set `possibleDuplicateOf`** \u2014 soft-duplicate match id (same Soundex + postcode, different identity; null if `sharesHousehold`).\n11. **Set `namesakeCount`** \u2014 count of same first+last name.\n12. **Set `memberId`** \u2014 built code (region + fiscal year + hash + Luhn check digit), de-duplicated against existing member ids.\n13. **Set `membershipCap`** \u2014 one above max membership level among household peers.\n14. **Set `capacityWarning`** \u2014 true if city holds 40\u201349 owners.\n\n## Phase 4 \u2014 Persist (`saveOwner`, its own transaction)\n\n15. **`@PrePersist` `defaultRegistrationDate()`**: defaults `registrationDate` to today if null, then rolls it to the next business day. (Note: the value persisted here can differ from the request value used in step 7.)\n16. **INSERT** via repository `save`.\n17. **`@PostPersist` `OwnerAuditListener.onCreate`**: emits three synchronous log entries \u2014 a human-readable audit line, a JSON audit event (`OWNER_CREATED`, with a sequence counter), and a \"welcome owner\" notification line.\n\n## Phase 5 \u2014 Response\n\n18. **Map** entity \u2192 `OwnerDto` (computes derived response fields: displayName, initials, membership level/points, segment, links, etc.).\n19. **Set `bulkSignupWarning`** on the DTO (true if >80 owners registered today) \u2014 response-only, not persisted.\n20. **Set `Location` header** to `/api/owners/{id}` and return **201 Created**.\n\n---\n\n**Notable behavioral points:**\n- The validator *mutates* `telephone`/`email`/`address`, so persisted values differ from raw input.\n- The uniqueness/limit checks (429, 409) run against an in-memory snapshot read in a *separate* transaction from the save \u2014 a TOCTOU gap, with no DB unique constraint backing `memberId`/identity.\n- `HouseholdDuplicates.isRejectedDuplicate` exists but is **not** called \u2014 only `assignHousehold` is.\n- The controller method itself is not `@Transactional`; only the read and the save are individually transactional."
